# Bivvy documentation maintenance

Bivvy documentation is **English-only** under `docs/`. It must stay synchronized with the code.

## When you change the product

In the **same change** (commit/PR), update the matching docs:

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Structure / new service | `docs/README.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, new `docs/services/*.md` |
| HTTP routes / payloads | `docs/api/*.md` + service page |
| Auth / security / env | `docs/security.md`, `docs/getting-started.md`, `.env.example` |
| Mobile UI / copy / brand | `docs/mobile/ui-and-brand.md`, `docs/mobile/overview.md` |
| Tests / CI / Docker | `docs/testing.md`, `docs/ci-cd.md` |

Follow the checklist in `docs/DOCUMENTATION.md`.

## Rules

- Do **not** document secrets; use placeholders only.
- Mark unfinished work as **Planned** or **Bootstrap** — never as shipped.
- Keep root `README.md` short; deep content belongs in `docs/`.
- Root `ARCHITECTURE.md` is only a pointer — edit `docs/architecture.md`.
- Bump **Last reviewed** on `docs/README.md` when you make a meaningful docs pass.
- Product UI strings and client API messages remain in English (US).
